---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import CTA from '../components/CTA.astro';
const schema=[{'@context':'https://schema.org','@type':'Service',name:'Restaurant operations and funding advisory',provider:{'@type':'Organization',name:'Tidewater Advisory LLC'},areaServed:['Washington, DC','Maryland','Virginia','Charlottesville, Virginia']}];
---
<Base title="Restaurant Advisory | Funding, Operations & Implementation | Tidewater" description="Identify restaurant grants and incentives across the DMV and Charlottesville. Improve purchasing, inventory, labor and food waste; implement projects from assessment through measurable results." schema={schema}>
  <section class="restaurant-hero section"><div class="container restaurant-hero-grid">
    <div><p class="eyebrow">Tidewater Advisory / 02 Restaurant Advisory</p><h1>Make the operation better.</h1><p class="lead">Find the funding. Protect the margin. Put improvements into practice.</p><p>For independent restaurants, hospitality groups and food businesses across Washington, DC, Maryland, Northern Virginia and the Charlottesville region.</p><div class="actions"><a class="button" href="/restaurant-advisory/funding">Explore grants & incentives ↗</a><a class="button-quiet" href="/contact">Discuss an improvement project ↗</a></div></div>
    <figure class="restaurant-hero-visual"><picture><source type="image/webp" srcset="/assets/tidal-oysters-640.webp 640w"/><img src="/assets/tidal-oysters.jpg" width="640" height="480" alt="Tidal water flowing around a cluster of oysters." fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"/></picture><figcaption>Small improvements compound. Like water finding the better channel.</figcaption></figure>
  </div></section>
  <section class="section"><div class="container"><div class="editorial-heading"><p class="eyebrow">What we do</p><h2>Three ways to unlock value.</h2><p class="lead">From the first question through the last implementation milestone.</p></div>
    <div class="grid-3">
      <article class="advisory-panel"><span class="step-number">01 / Capital & support</span><h3>Funding & incentives</h3><p>Research and qualify grants, public programs, utility rebates and other incentives. Translate eligibility rules into a scoped project, application and practical delivery plan.</p><a class="link-arrow" href="/restaurant-advisory/funding">Browse opportunities ↗</a></article>
      <article class="advisory-panel"><span class="step-number">02 / Margin protection</span><h3>Operational performance</h3><p>Review purchasing, recipes, yields, inventory, prep, labor deployment and equipment. Identify the handful of changes most likely to return real value.</p><a class="link-arrow" href="/contact">Request an assessment ↗</a></article>
      <article class="advisory-panel"><span class="step-number">03 / Stewardship & savings</span><h3>Food waste & recovery</h3><p>Start upstream: prevent overbuying, spoilage and avoidable prep waste. Then build appropriate donation and resource-recovery systems with qualified partners.</p><a class="link-arrow" href="/restaurant-advisory/food-waste">Read the food waste playbook ↗</a></article>
    </div></div></section>
  <section class="section reverse method-section"><div class="container"><div class="editorial-heading"><p class="eyebrow">Our operating method</p><h2>Assess. Fund. Implement.</h2><p class="lead">No handoff after a report. Tidewater stays with the project through coordination and measurement.</p></div><div class="grid-3"><div class="panel"><span class="step-number">01 / Establish the baseline</span><h3>Find the constraint.</h3><p>Understand current processes and real economics. Prioritize opportunities worth a manager's time.</p></div><div class="panel"><span class="step-number">02 / Build the business case</span><h3>Make the numbers work.</h3><p>Validate funding eligibility, investment, payback assumptions, partners, and timelines before committing.</p></div><div class="panel"><span class="step-number">03 / Execute & measure</span><h3>See the work through.</h3><p>Coordinate vendors, people and milestones; measure outcomes against the agreed baseline.</p></div></div></div></section>
  <section class="section"><div class="container grid-2 restaurant-bottom-cta"><div><p class="eyebrow">Funding intelligence</p><h2>Find funding for your next improvement.</h2><p>We track relevant programs across the District, Maryland and Virginia—including Charlottesville and Central Virginia. Each opportunity shows eligibility caveats, official source, application status and when it was checked.</p><a class="button" href="/restaurant-advisory/funding">Browse the funding desk ↗</a></div><div class="panel"><p class="eyebrow">Tidewater Food Waste</p><h3>Waste less. Give more back.</h3><p>Our food waste program is now part of Restaurant Advisory: prevention first, then donation and resource recovery with qualified partners. Tidewater provides advisory and project management; we do not operate collection, hauling, composting or disposal.</p><a class="link-arrow" href="/restaurant-advisory/food-waste">Food waste & resource recovery ↗</a></div></div></section>
  <CTA title="An improvement is only valuable when it sticks." body="Start with a scoped conversation about the project, its economics, and who must deliver it." href="/contact" label="Discuss your operation" />
</Base>
